From 777331dce7c93005df1d85a9b76f1abd85e0a118 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:20:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 78/79] arm64: dts: qcom: baldur: WCN7860 WAKE# is active low

PCIe WAKE# is an open-drain, active-low signal: the endpoint pulls it low
to request a wake and it idles high. Describing it as GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH makes
drivers/pci/of.c arm a level wake IRQ that fires while the line idles high
-- the tablet woke about 2.5 s into every s2idle (pm_wakeup_irq = msmgpio 104),
so the root port wakeup had to be disabled from userspace. The same fix is
under review for the Kaanapali MTP board.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-wifi.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-wifi.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-wifi.dtsi
index 4dced6128..f7b2de18b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-wifi.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-wifi.dtsi
@@ -198,7 +198,7 @@ &pcie0_phy {
 };
 
 &pcie_port0 {
-	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 102 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 	wifi@0 {
-- 
2.43.0

